            "the fy2025 10-k materially expands the severity language in the customer-concentration risk factor. in s1, the apple mdm paragraph only stated that to the extent apple takes share from customers of qualcomm's integrated modem+ap products, revenues could be negatively impacted. in s2, qualcomm adds that it expects apple to increasingly use its own modem products in future devices, \"which will have a significant negative impact on our qct revenues, results of operations and cash flows\" — a new, quantifiable severity statement absent in s1. the underlying customer-concentration warning on premium-tier devices and chinese oems is largely retained, but the apple modem-transition severity is new disclosure. remaining risk-factor wording (customer/licensee concentration, premium-tier reliance) is otherwise substantially unchanged."
          ],
          "classification": "changed",
