            291288,
            "changed",
            "named counterparties in the customer-vertical-integration risk factor broadened. s1 named only \"samsung\" as the example of largest customers developing their own integrated circuits, with a separate detailed apple description (intel modem assets, competitor modem usage). s2 names \"apple, samsung and xiaomi\" as developing their own integrated circuit products and states plainly that qualcomm expects these customers to use their own products in some or all future devices. xiaomi is newly added as a named counterparty, and the apple-specific narrative was consolidated. this is a changed, expanded scope of the customer-concentration risk rather than an entirely new exposure, since s1 already warned that largest customers could vertically integrate and already named apple and samsung."
          ],
